{
	title: 'Installer: ./install puts hal on the PATH',
	spec: './install (bash, repo root) sets up a checkout, doing only what is missing, safe to run again. It shows a checklist ([x] done, [ ] missing): bun (on PATH or ~/.bun/bin), bun install (node_modules), ~/.local/bin/hal as a symlink to this checkout\'s run, ~/.local/bin in PATH. Everything done: it says "Everything in order. Start with: hal" and exits. Otherwise it asks once "Set up Hal? [Y/n]" (-y answers yes; any other option is refused with exit 1 before anything changes), then: Bun through the official curl https://bun.sh/install | bash; bun install --cwd <checkout>; the symlink (ln -sfn, replacing a link to another checkout); the PATH line appended with a "# Added by hal installer" comment to the login shell\'s config (zsh ~/.zshenv, bash ~/.bash_profile on macOS or ~/.bashrc, fish ~/.config/fish/config.fish with fish_add_path; other shells get the line printed), skipped when the config already mentions .local/bin outside comments. It ends with how to start (hal, after a new shell when PATH changed). Deliberately minimal, unlike the old Hal installer (artifact old-install): no git, ripgrep, Homebrew, config file or local-only mode. Test (src/install.test.ts) in a temp HOME: link and one PATH line, a second run adds nothing, a PATH with the bin dir is in order, an unknown option changes nothing. ./run runs ./install first when node_modules is missing, saying "Dependencies are missing (<path>/node_modules): running ./install first."; without dependencies Hal would start but its web client could not build. On a terminal, every start whose first frame is inline (fits the screen and is not full mode) paints one blank row above it, so it does not touch the shell output above (render.state.gap, set by main.initTerminal). A start that never paints, such as hal -r failing with no remembered host, adds no blank line.',
	status: 'done',
	notes: [
		'Bug fix: ./run echoed the blank line before bun started, so hal -r errors printed after an empty line. Invariant restored: the blank row belongs to the first inline paint; output without a frame (errors, ./run auth) starts right under the shell prompt.'
